  "narrative": [
    {
      "text": "On the Palais-Smale condition in geometric knot theory — We prove that various families of energies relevant in geometric knot theory satisfy the Palais–Smale condition (PS) on submanifolds of\n\n**On the Palais-Smale condition in geometric knot theory**\n\n*Nicolas Freches, Henrik Schumacher, Daniel Steenebrügge, and Heiko von der Mosel*\n\n52 pp, 22 sections.\n\n**Abstract.** We prove that various families of energies relevant in geometric knot theory satisfy the Palais–Smale condition (PS) on submanifolds of arclength parametrized knots. These energies include linear combinations of the Euler-Bernoulli bending energy with a wide variety of non-local knot energies, such as O’Hara’s self-repulsive potentials 𝐸𝛼,𝑝, gen- eralized tangent-point energies TP( 𝑝,𝑞), and generalized integral Menger curvature func- tionals intM( 𝑝,𝑞). Even the tangent-point energies TP( 𝑝,2) for 𝑝∈(4, 5) alone are shown to fulfill the (PS)-condition. For all energies mentioned we can therefore prove existence of minimizing knots in any prescribed ambient isotopy class, and we provide long-time existence of their Hilbert-gradient flows, and subconvergence to critical knots as time goes to infinity.\n\n**Outline.** The Palais–Smale condition; Introduction; Three families of knot energies on curves; Main results; Outline of the paper; The Palais–Smale condition in an abstract sett; Energies on submanifolds of Hilbert spaces; Gradient flows on Riemannian manifolds; The submanifolds of arclength parametrized cur; The arclength manifolds N1+s and A1+s; The topology of arclength manifolds; Critical knots in arclength submanifolds; The Palais–Smale condition for bending energy ; Bending energy with self-avoidance term; Tangent-point energy; Regularity of critical points; Bending energy; Bending energy with tangent-point energy",
      "lang": "en",
